## Why this is separate from LICENSE

The code in this repository is MIT. MIT is a software licence: its attribution
clause is written around distributing copies of a program, and it does not
answer cleanly what "the above copyright notice" means when someone lifts three
paragraphs of a standard into their own handbook.

The point of publishing these standards is that other people take the prose.
CC BY says how to credit it. Attribution is the only thing asked for.
